# Scratch build and tooling output, plus artifacts/notes - the working notes and
# findings for whatever is in flight. Notes expire when their work lands: promote
# verified durable content to the org /docs repository, then delete the local
# copy. ccpwgl has no docs/ tree of its own.
artifacts/

# test fixtures containing real extracted CCP/EVE game assets (.black, .sm_hi,
# and .webgl.cewg packages built from them) - not safe to commit
test/fixtures/

# Working notes stay local - durable content belongs in the org /docs tree
NOTES-*.md
src/**/README.md

# Agent entry files: generated per checkout, never committed
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md

# Guards against notes landing back in the root rather than artifacts/notes
AGENT-*.md
PLAN-*.md

# `docs/` used to be ignored by that same guard. It should not have been: the
# rule exists to stop scratch notes littering the root, and it also blocked the
# only legitimate home for knowledge that belongs to THIS repository. With
# nowhere tracked to put a durable finding, findings went to gitignored scratch
# instead - five separate stores of it, none backed up, one of them holding the
# organisation's flow-of-authority rule.
#
# docs/ is now TRACKED and curated. Scratch still belongs in artifacts/notes/
# and still expires when its work lands; see docs/README.md for which is which.

# Scratch harnesses that need external state (a fetched asset, a running
# service) so they cannot join the test sweep
*.local.js
*.local.mjs
*.local.cjs
